// effects.def -- the cosmetic effect channel.

//
// A CHANNEL is a closed set of named messages, each carrying a payload, each
// dispatched to exactly one handler. `channel` declares the shared payload; its
// fields are prepended to every member and serialize first, exactly as
// `Entity :: base` works for entities. A member names the channel as its
// declaration kind and carries a mandatory description -- these are the names of
// a closed protocol, and the description feeds the generated enum comments and
// --scaffold's stubs.
//
// One channel per file. The kind enum is DERIVED from declaration order, so
// nothing is spelled twice, and ORDER IS THE WIRE ID -- mixed into SCHEMA_HASH,
// so a reorder is a refused handshake rather than a silent remap. Append.
//
// f32 and v3 ride the wire QUANTIZED (network::write_coord). A field that needs
// full float precision does not belong on this wire.
//
// Nothing here imports anything and nothing may import this file: an effect
// references no entity, no asset and no cvar.
//
// Unreliable: the batch rides its own S2C_EffectBatch message. Lost =
// invisible. You will not notice a missing explosion under packet loss.

Effect :: channel
{
    origin:           v3    // where it happened, world space
    normal:           v3    // {0,0,0} = not applicable
    color:            v3
    scale:            f32
    attached_entity:  u32   // an entity uid; 0 = world-space
    surface_material: u16   // 0 = unknown
}

Rocket_Explosion :: Effect  "splash particles + surface decal"
Bullet_Impact    :: Effect  "world-surface hit"
Footstep         :: Effect  "one foot planting"
Jump             :: Effect  "leaving the ground"
Land             :: Effect  "arriving back on it"
Flesh_Impact     :: Effect  "a shot that landed on a player; surface_material carries the hit_region_t, attached_entity the victim"
